      "writtenOn": "2025-09-29T14:19:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you have `KEEP_TARGET_FILES\u003dy`, and there already exists a signed target files zip in the output directory, it will not overwrite it, correct, but will simply skip the `sign_target_files_apks` step. Bear in mind that if the previous signing session was interrupted or failed, it might not clean up after itself, leaving a broken zip in place, so this should be used with caution, e.g. when you know that only the OTA generation failed last time or something.",
